// Annex C.16 lists `connectrules` among the ten keywords "not used by
// Verilog-A", and closes with "NOTE—All keywords of Verilog-AMS HDL are
// reserved words for Verilog-A": not used is not the same as free, so it may
// not serve as an identifier. Annex B Table B.1 lists it too.
//
// Its own file rather than an arm of 16: a `//! reject` substring is matched
// against every diagnostic of the file, and `connectrules` is a substring of
// `endconnectrules` — next to that spelling the arm is satisfied whether or not
// `connectrules` itself was ever flagged. Here it is the only keyword in the
// file, so nothing else can satisfy it. The module is named
// `annex_c_reserved_spelling_31`, not after the keyword, for the same reason:
// a diagnostic quoting the module name must not satisfy the arm.
//
// Reserving the spelling is a different rule from refusing the CONSTRUCT; the
// `connectrules ... endconnectrules` declaration itself is 24.
//
//! lrm C.16
//! lrm B
//! reject E0208
//! reject connectrules
module annex_c_reserved_spelling_31;
    real connectrules;
endmodule
